<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},<br />
<br />
Your Service Dog, &lt;<strong>DOG NAME</strong>&gt; has been granted permission to travel with you in the aircraft cabin with Qantas, while your current Handler Identification remains valid.<br />
<br />
<strong>Preparing for travel</strong><br />
<br />
Follow these simple tips to ensure your journey with us is hassle-free as possible:
<ul>
	<li>Bring your identity documents in your carry-on baggage, such as a current identity card issued by your training organisation or trainer.</li>
	<li>Your Service Dog should wear its harness, vest, coat and/or medallion to identify it as a Service Dog.</li>
	<li>On the aircraft, your Service Dog is to be seated on the floor in the space allocated by Qantas (generally adjacent to your seat). Qantas will provide a moisture absorbent mat, and your Service Dog is to be secured by its leash to the aircraft seat leg, seat track ring or other tether point approved by Qantas.</li>
	<li>Ensure that you follow the directions of the crew who will provide relevant instructions in the interests of safety.</li>
	<li>Review the <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/specific-needs/travelling-with-specific-needs/service-dogs/conditions-of-carriage.html">Service Dogs Conditions of Carriage</a>&nbsp;for more information.</li>
</ul>
<strong>Future travel with your Service Dog</strong><br />
<br />
For each future booking, once your flight(s) have been confirmed, please <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/specific-needs/contact-us-about-specific-needs.html?int_cam=au%3Aspecific-needs%3Aarticle%3Acontact-us-about-specific-needs%3Aen%3Ann#helpline">contact us</a> to ensure that Qantas has noted the details of your upcoming flights and can make the appropriate seating arrangements for you and your Service Dog. Qantas will request current Handler Identification from you if it has expired since your previous travel.<br />
<br />
<strong>If you are travelling internationally</strong><br />
<br />
To acknowledge destination specific requirements, please ensure that you complete and return the International Travel Declaration Form &nbsp;if you have not already done so. The <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/specific-needs/travelling-with-specific-needs/service-dogs.html">International Travel Declaration Form</a> must be completed for each international booking. Bring your quarantine related documentation (including inoculation certificates and entry permits) in your carry-on baggage to ensure your Service Dog can lawfully depart the country of origin and be cleared for entry into the country of arrival.<br />
<br />
We look forward to welcoming you and your Service Dog onboard.</body>
</html>